      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.55,
      "end_seconds": 240.55,
      "duration_seconds": 10.0,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now heavy periods with iron deficiency is my leading thought, not anything worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.15,
      "end_seconds": 279.51,
      "duration_seconds": 31.36,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a blood count for heavy periods. I'd like you to take tranexamic acid, 1 gram, three times a day during periods, for four days each cycle. You take it by mouth. That should help with heavy periods. Iron can darken the stools and bother the stomach, so take it after food. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.56,
      "end_seconds": 295.14,
      "duration_seconds": 14.58,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: you soak through pads hourly or feel faint. In that case don't wait. Book a review after the results. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
